REM Regression test for issue #14: non-ASCII/UTF-8 bytes are silently
REM dropped rather than sent as garbage keycodes. "ı" (U+0131, Turkish
REM dotless i) encodes as the two UTF-8 bytes 0xC4 0xB1; neither byte is
REM < 128 so char_to_hid_usage() maps both to usage 0 and no report is
REM emitted for them. The surrounding ASCII characters must still be
REM typed normally.
STRING aıb
